{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01305",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 5.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.12,
      "end_seconds": 10.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.35,
      "end_seconds": 25.27,
      "duration_seconds": 13.92,
      "text": "Mainly a sore ankle. There's a couple of other things, um, but that's the main one. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.79,
      "end_seconds": 31.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.35,
      "end_seconds": 37.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Right, for about three months, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.37,
      "end_seconds": 48.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.48,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.7,
      "end_seconds": 63.63,
      "duration_seconds": 13.93,
      "text": "Okay, so only rest and ice, and it's not much. Walking definitely sets it off. A little swelling was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.16,
      "end_seconds": 68.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.58,
      "end_seconds": 77.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Ibuprofen gel, three times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.33,
      "end_seconds": 93.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.1,
      "end_seconds": 103.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Uh, you know, no, nothing I can think of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.39,
      "end_seconds": 107.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "So, have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.58,
      "end_seconds": 112.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Trimethoprim. I come out in... well, itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.67,
      "end_seconds": 120.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.69,
      "end_seconds": 126.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Uh, my cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.64,
      "end_seconds": 130.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.4,
      "end_seconds": 144.83,
      "duration_seconds": 13.43,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital. I hardly move around during the day. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.11,
      "end_seconds": 149.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "And what about crack or pop or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.77,
      "end_seconds": 156.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Let me think, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.07,
      "end_seconds": 160.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Any sign of pain in the foot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.18,
      "end_seconds": 169.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "No pain in the foot, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.75,
      "end_seconds": 176.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.1,
      "end_seconds": 178.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.66,
      "end_seconds": 184.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.3,
      "end_seconds": 200.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.84,
      "end_seconds": 233.41,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 113 over 74, pulse is 74 beats a minute, SpO2 99 percent on room air. And temp 37.0 degrees, respiratory rate 15."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.99,
      "end_seconds": 238.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.57,
      "end_seconds": 243.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.0,
      "end_seconds": 263.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.63,
      "text": "There's mild swelling over the outside of the ankle, and you can put your weight on it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.4,
      "end_seconds": 270.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.96,
      "end_seconds": 291.05,
      "duration_seconds": 12.09,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with a mild ankle sprain at this stage. Another possibility is a minor fracture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.89,
      "end_seconds": 293.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.24,
      "end_seconds": 310.31,
      "duration_seconds": 15.07,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a mild ankle sprain, and we'll watch how it goes. Rest, ice, a compression bandage and keep it raised for two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.86,
      "end_seconds": 329.47,
      "duration_seconds": 18.61,
      "text": "I follow. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. Let's review you if it is not better in two weeks. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.02,
      "end_seconds": 333.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}